  {
   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Top-Down Letters\n\nLetters descend from above in a pronounced staircase, one symbol at a time, with no blur: a sharp, graphic title.\n\nCategory: typography. Length: 2 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- A single uppercase word or short acronym should enter with structural weight, each letter landing like a stamp.\n- The scene calls for a sharp, graphic title card where the sequential drop reinforces the rhythm of the word.\n\nAvoid when:\n- The text is more than about 8 characters: use staggered-fade-up for longer phrases.\n- You want blur or softness on entry: use soft-blur-in.\n- The letters should rise from below: use bottom-up-letters.\n\nVariables:\n- text (string): Text, default \"Signal\"\n- stagger_delay (number, 1-12): Stagger delay, default 3\n- distance (number, 0-200): Distance, default 46\n- font_size (number, 12-220): Font size, default 72\n- color (color): Color, default \"#171717\"\n- font_weight (enum): Font weight, default \"600\"\n- speed (number, 0.25-4): Speed, default 1\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
  {
   "path": "scene.html",
   "role": "source",
   "content": "<!doctype html>\n<!--\n  Top-Down Letters\n\n  Letters descend from above in a pronounced staircase, one symbol at a time.\n\n  Ported to an HTML + GSAP sub-composition by usemosio/blocks from:\n  https://github.com/Remocn/remocn/blob/126221ae00ba86eb40b65731b125ff398687d3b7/registry/remocn/top-down-letters/index.tsx\n\n  MIT License\n\n  Copyright (c) 2026 Remocn\n\n  Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy\n  of this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal\n  in the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights\n  to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell\n  copies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is\n  furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n\n  The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all\n  copies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\n  THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR\n  IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,\n  FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE\n  AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER\n  LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,\n  OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE\n  SOFTWARE.\n-->\n<html\n  lang=\"en\"\n  data-composition-id=\"top-down-letters\"\n  data-composition-duration=\"2\"\n  data-composition-variables='[\n    {\"id\": \"text\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Text\", \"description\": \"Word or short acronym that drops in.\", \"default\": \"Signal\"},\n    {\"id\": \"stagger_delay\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Stagger delay\", \"description\": \"Frames (30 per second) between one letter and the next.\", \"default\": 3, \"min\": 1, \"max\": 12, \"step\": 1, \"unit\": \"frames\"},\n    {\"id\": \"distance\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Distance\", \"description\": \"How far above its place each letter starts.\", \"default\": 46, \"min\": 0, \"max\": 200, \"step\": 1, \"unit\": \"px\"},\n    {\"id\": \"font_size\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Font size\", \"description\": \"Maximum text size in pixels. Longer text shrinks to fit the frame.\", \"default\": 72, \"min\": 12, \"max\": 220, \"step\": 1, \"unit\": \"px\"},\n    {\"id\": \"color\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Color\", \"description\": \"Text color.\", \"default\": \"#171717\"},\n    {\"id\": \"font_weight\", \"type\": \"enum\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Font weight\", \"description\": \"Weight of the text.\", \"default\": \"600\", \"options\": [{\"value\": \"400\", \"label\": \"Regular\"}, {\"value\": \"500\", \"label\": \"Medium\"}, {\"value\": \"600\", \"label\": \"Semibold\"}, {\"value\": \"700\", \"label\": \"Bold\"}]},\n    {\"id\": \"speed\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Speed\", \"description\": \"Playback speed multiplier.\", \"default\": 1, \"min\": 0.25, \"max\": 4, \"step\": 0.05, \"unit\": \"x\"}\n  ]'\n>\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <title>Top-Down Letters</title>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <template>\n      <link\n        rel=\"stylesheet\"\n        href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Geist:wght@400;500;600;700&amp;display=block\"\n      />\n      <style>\n        #root {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n          overflow: hidden;\n          container-type: size;\n          pointer-events: none;\n          color: var(--color, #171717);\n          font-family: var(--font-display, Geist, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, sans-serif);\n        }\n        .tdl-stage { position: absolute; inset: 0; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; }\n        .tdl-line { letter-spacing: -0.05em; line-height: 1; white-space: pre; }\n        .tdl-char { display: inline-block; white-space: pre; opacity: 0; backface-visibility: hidden; transform-origin: 50% 55%; }\n      </style>\n\n      <div id=\"root\" data-composition-id=\"top-down-letters\" data-duration=\"2\" data-fps=\"30\">\n        <div id=\"tdl-clip\" class=\"tdl-stage clip\" data-start=\"0\" data-duration=\"2\" data-track-index=\"0\">\n          <span id=\"tdl-line\" class=\"tdl-line\" role=\"img\"></span>\n        </div>\n\n        <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.14.2/dist/gsap.min.js\"></script>\n        <script>\n          (function () {\n            \"use strict\";\n            var root = document.getElementById(\"root\");\n            var vars =\n              window.__hyperframes && window.__hyperframes.getVariables\n                ? window.__hyperframes.getVariables()\n                : {};\n\n            function num(value, fallback, min, max) {\n              var n = Number(value);\n              return Number.isFinite(n) ? Math.min(max, Math.max(min, n)) : fallback;\n            }\n            function str(value, fallback) {\n              return typeof value === \"string\" && value.trim() ? value : fallback;\n            }\n            function pick(value, list, fallback) {\n              return list.indexOf(String(value)) >= 0 ? String(value) : fallback;\n            }\n            function bool(value, fallback) {\n              return typeof value === \"boolean\" ? value : value === \"true\" ? true : value === \"false\" ? false : fallback;\n            }\n            // Easing.bezier(x1, y1, x2, y2) as a function of t (Newton, then bisection).\n            function bez(x1, y1, x2, y2) {\n              function cx(s) { return 3 * x1 * s * (1 - s) * (1 - s) + 3 * x2 * s * s * (1 - s) + s * s * s; }\n              function cy(s) { return 3 * y1 * s * (1 - s) * (1 - s) + 3 * y2 * s * s * (1 - s) + s * s * s; }\n              return function (t) {\n                if (t <= 0) return 0;\n                if (t >= 1) return 1;\n                var lo = 0, hi = 1, s = t;\n                for (var i = 0; i < 40; i++) {\n                  var x = cx(s);\n                  if (Math.abs(x - t) < 1e-6) break;\n                  if (x < t) lo = s; else hi = s;\n                  s = (lo + hi) / 2;\n                }\n                return cy(s);\n              };\n            }\n            // interpolate(f, [a, b], [from, to]) with both ends clamped, like the source framework's extrapolate \"clamp\".\n            function interp(f, a, b, from, to, ease) {\n              var t = b === a ? 1 : Math.min(1, Math.max(0, (f - a) / (b - a)));\n              return from + (to - from) * (ease ? ease(t) : t);\n            }\n            // Fit one line to 90 % of the frame width: shrinks the font size when it overflows.\n            function fit(root, line, size) {\n              line.style.fontSize = size + \"px\";\n              var maxWidth = Math.max(1, root.clientWidth * 0.9);\n              if (line.scrollWidth > maxWidth) {\n                size = Math.max(12, size * (maxWidth / line.scrollWidth));\n                line.style.fontSize = size + \"px\";\n              }\n              return size;\n            }\n            // Drives draw(frame) from the paused timeline: frame = time * 30 * speed (the source framework's useCurrentFrame() * speed).\n            function drive(tl, total, speed, draw) {\n              var clock = { t: 0 };\n              tl.to(clock, { t: total, duration: total, ease: \"none\", onUpdate: function () { draw(clock.t * 30 * speed); } }, 0);\n              draw(0);\n            }\n\n            var text = str(vars.text, \"Signal\");\n            var stagger = num(vars.stagger_delay, 3, 1, 12);\n            var distance = num(vars.distance, 46, 0, 200);\n            var speed = num(vars.speed, 1, 0.25, 4);\n            var line = document.getElementById(\"tdl-line\");\n            line.style.fontWeight = pick(vars.font_weight, [\"400\", \"500\", \"600\", \"700\"], \"600\");\n            line.setAttribute(\"aria-label\", text);\n            if (typeof vars.color === \"string\" && vars.color) root.style.setProperty(\"--color\", vars.color);\n            var chars = Array.from(text).map(function (ch, i) {\n              var span = document.createElement(\"span\");\n              span.id = \"tdl-char-\" + i;\n              span.className = \"tdl-char\";\n              span.textContent = ch;\n              line.appendChild(span);\n              return span;\n            });\n            fit(root, line, num(vars.font_size, 72, 12, 220));\n\n            // remocn: 12-frame fade, 7-frame drop from above, one letter every `stagger` frames.\n            var ease = bez(0.18, 1, 0.32, 1);\n            function draw(frame) {\n              chars.forEach(function (el, i) {\n                var local = frame - i * stagger;\n                el.style.opacity = interp(local, 0, 12, 0, 1, ease);\n                el.style.transform = \"translateY(\" + interp(local, 0, 7, -distance, 0, ease) + \"px)\";\n              });\n            }\n            var total = parseFloat(root.dataset.duration || \"2\");\n            var tl = gsap.timeline({ paused: true });\n            drive(tl, total, speed, draw);\n            if (tl.duration() < total) tl.to({}, { duration: total - tl.duration() });\n            tl.seek(0);\n            window.__timelines = window.__timelines || {};\n            window.__timelines[\"top-down-letters\"] = tl;\n          })();\n        </script>\n      </div>\n    </template>\n  </body>\n</html>\n"
  }
 ],
